§3 THE CORRIDOR (§34.5, Register 1309 / 1350 / 1460): L(Z) < a < U(Z) from nu_g < nu_r for every admissible rival
====================================================================================================
  CONVENTIONS named: candidate subshells (n,l) with n <= N_MAX, l <= min(n-1, 3); a rival is admissible at step Z iff its occupancy at Z-1 is
  below 2(2l+1); the entrant g is the differentiating subshell of §2; form A (1309): p = n-l-1; form B (1350): p = n-l-1 + q/2(2l+1) with q the
  occupancy at Z-1; the inequality nu_g < nu_r is a(sqrt p_r - sqrt p_g) < n_r - n_g; a bound is an endpoint Dn/(sqrt p_r - sqrt p_g);
  sqrt p_r == sqrt p_g requires n_r > n_g (violated -> the corridor is empty); L = max of lower bounds, U = min of upper bounds; NON-EMPTY iff L < U.
