====================================================================================================
§5 THE MEMORYLESS TEST (§34.6 "104 of 106"; Register 1332; docket 37 / 1448 "vacuous") — one named reconstruction
====================================================================================================
  CONVENTION (reconstruction): at each Z, for every admissible candidate c (the entrant included), build c's own corridor as if c were the entrant;
  set a = the midpoint of (L_c, U_c) when both are finite, L_c + 1 or U_c - 1 when one is infinite ("its own crossing value" read as an interior point of its own corridor;
  a placement AT the endpoint ties c with the rival that defines it and can never be strict-least — self-caught, rewritten); c is SELF-CONSISTENT iff at that a its nu is least (strict) among admissibles.
  self-consistent candidates per step (count: steps): {3: 29, 4: 33, 5: 28, 6: 14, 7: 2} | steps with 2..4: 62 of 106 | observed among them: 106 of 106
  VERDICT 1332 "104 of 106 admit two to four; the observed always among them": MEASURED differs under this convention — docket 37 already records the figure as not reconstructible from the stated convention; the record stands (G0c)

